From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 53/55] scp: do not append a resumed tail to a file that
 changed

The "scp -Z" sink hashes the destination when it receives the record and
appends the tail only when all of it has arrived, possibly much later. The
sender had checked the first orig_size bytes against its own file, so if
something else wrote to the destination in between, the tail went on a file
that was no longer the one that was checked, and the result matched neither.

Before appending, check that the file still has the size it had. If not,
report it, leave the file alone and remove the temporary tail.
---
 scp.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scp.c b/scp.c
index fff4a4484..d1e1297c9 100644
--- a/scp.c
+++ b/scp.c
@@ -1980,6 +1980,7 @@ resume_append(const char *tail, const char *orig, off_t orig_size, int wrerr)
 	char res_buf[512]; /* set at 512 just because, might want to increase*/
 	size_t res_bytes;
 	int cat_ok = 0;
+	struct stat st;
 
 	if (wrerr) {
 		/*
@@ -1987,6 +1988,15 @@ resume_append(const char *tail, const char *orig, off_t orig_size, int wrerr)
 		 * corrupt the existing file, so leave that alone. The error
 		 * has already been recorded.
 		 */
+	} else if (stat(orig, &st) == 0 && st.st_size != orig_size) {
+		/*
+		 * The sender checked the first orig_size bytes of this file
+		 * against its own and sent the rest. The file has changed since
+		 * the sink looked at it, so the tail would not belong on it.
+		 */
+		note_err("%s: changed while it was being resumed (%lld bytes, "
+		    "was %lld); the tail was not appended", orig,
+		    (long long)st.st_size, (long long)orig_size);
 	} else if ((of = fopen(orig, "a")) == NULL) {
 		note_err("%s: could not open for appending: %s",
 		    orig, strerror(errno));
-- 
